IMPORT prelude

-- National Cadet Corps Act 1972 (Singapore) -- who may be enrolled as a cadet (s 8), the Corps' place outside the Singapore Armed
-- Forces (s 4(3)), resignation and revocation of officers' appointments (s 9(4), (5)), dismissal of cadets (s 11), summary
-- discipline of cadets and its punishments (ss 12, 13), boards of inquiry for officers (s 14), compensation for death or injury
-- (s 15), the bar on tort claims for injuries to members (s 16), and the weapons-Acts exemption (s 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/NCCA1972.txt. The revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the latest
-- amendments annotated are Act 5 of 2025 (s 5(1), (1A), wef 9 March 2025) and Act 31 of 2023 (the s 2 definition of "permanent
-- resident of Singapore", wef 1 December 2025). The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is out of step by one
-- (it numbers "Short title" as 2); this file follows the section numbers in the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0135 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to -- here a schoolchild cadet, a teacher-officer,
-- a volunteer instructor, or a parent. No scenario has asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets.
-- Not encoded: the raising and organisation of the Corps (ss 3, 4(1), (2), (4)), the Council and Commandant's appointment and
-- powers (ss 5, 6, 7), secondment of SAF personnel (s 10), and the regulation-making power (s 18). The regulations themselves
-- (age limits, enrolment periods, the summary procedure, compensation amounts) were not retrieved, so every rule here that the Act
-- makes "subject to the regulations" is encoded from the Act alone.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Cadet Corps Act 1972 -- cadets, officers and members`

§§ `8 -- eligibility to enrol`

-- s 8(1): "Subject to the provisions of this Act and the regulations made under this Act, any person who is a citizen of Singapore or
-- a permanent resident of Singapore is eligible to be enrolled as a cadet in the Corps."
-- (2): "The Minister may in special cases approve the enrolment of persons who are neither citizens of Singapore nor permanent
-- residents of Singapore in the Corps."
-- The Act sets no age and does not require the person to be a student; s 18(2)(d) leaves "the age and other qualifications for cadet
-- membership" to regulations (not retrieved).
GIVEN `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Minister's special approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is eligible to enrol as a cadet` IF
    `is a citizen` OR `is a permanent resident` OR `has the Minister's special approval`

§§ `4(3) -- not the armed forces`

-- s 4(3): "The Corps are to be affiliated to the Singapore Armed Forces for the purposes of training but members of the Corps are not
-- to be members of the Singapore Armed Forces."
-- Inference (not stated): an SAF serviceman seconded to the Corps under s 10 stays an SAF member by virtue of his SAF service, not
-- his Corps role; the Act does not say whether a seconded serviceman is a "member" of the Corps at all.
GIVEN `is a member of the Corps` IS A BOOLEAN, `is separately serving in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a member of the Singapore Armed Forces` IF
    `is separately serving in the Singapore Armed Forces`

§§ `9(4), (5) -- leaving an appointment as officer, honorary officer or honorary instructor`

-- s 9(4): an officer, honorary officer or honorary instructor "may, with the approval of the Minister, at any time resign from the
-- appointment." (5): "The Minister may, with or without assigning any reason, revoke the appointment".
-- A resignation without the Minister's approval does not end the appointment on the text; a revocation needs no reason.
GIVEN `resigned` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister approved the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister revoked it` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reason was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment has ended` IF
    (`resigned` AND `the Minister approved the resignation`) OR `the Minister revoked it`

§§ `11 -- discharge and dismissal of cadets`

-- s 11(1): "Subject to the regulations ..., every cadet may be discharged from the Corps on the expiry of the period for which the
-- cadet was enrolled." (2): "The Commandant may, on the recommendation of the commanding officer, dismiss any cadet." (3): "In the
-- case of a cadet who is a student of a school, the Commandant must obtain the concurrence of the principal of the school which the
-- cadet is enrolled in, for the dismissal of the cadet."
GIVEN `the enrolment period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cadet may be discharged` IF `the enrolment period has expired`

GIVEN `the commanding officer recommended dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN, `the cadet is a student of a school` IS A BOOLEAN, `the principal concurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commandant may dismiss the cadet` IF
    `the commanding officer recommended dismissal` AND ((NOT `the cadet is a student of a school`) OR `the principal concurs`)

§§ `12 -- what brings a cadet before the commanding officer`

-- s 12: "Any cadet who -- (a) in such manner as to show wilful defiance of authority, disobeys any lawful command given to the cadet
-- or conveyed to the cadet personally; or (b) contravenes any order or regulation made under this Act, being an order or a regulation
-- known to the cadet or which the cadet might reasonably be expected to know, must be dealt with summarily by the cadet's commanding
-- officer in the manner prescribed by regulations".
-- Plain disobedience without wilful defiance, or disobedience of an unlawful command, is not within (a).
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `disobeyed a command` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the command was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the command was given or conveyed personally` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contravened an order or regulation under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew the order or regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `might reasonably be expected to know it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cadet must be dealt with summarily` IF
        (    `the conduct`'s `disobeyed a command`
         AND `the conduct`'s `the command was lawful`
         AND `the conduct`'s `the command was given or conveyed personally`
         AND `the conduct`'s `in a manner showing wilful defiance of authority`)
    OR  (    `the conduct`'s `contravened an order or regulation under the Act`
         AND (`the conduct`'s `knew the order or regulation` OR `the conduct`'s `might reasonably be expected to know it`))

§§ `13 -- the commanding officer's punishments`

-- s 13: where a commanding officer deals with a case summarily, the commanding officer "may, if the commanding officer records a
-- finding of guilt, impose one or more of the following punishments: (a) reprimand; (b) where the cadet holds a rank, reduction in
-- rank; (c) suspension of membership in the Corps for a period not exceeding 3 months."
-- Dismissal is NOT on the list: only the Commandant may dismiss a cadet (s 11(2)). Nor is any fine or detention.
DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `reprimand`
    `reduction in rank`
    `suspension of membership`
    `dismissal from the Corps`
    `a fine`
    `detention`

GIVEN `the punishment` IS A Punishment, `a finding of guilt is recorded` IS A BOOLEAN, `the cadet holds a rank` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commanding officer may impose it` IF
    `a finding of guilt is recorded` AND
        CONSIDER `the punishment`
        WHEN `reprimand` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `reduction in rank` THEN `the cadet holds a rank`
        WHEN `suspension of membership` THEN `months of suspension` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months of suspension` AT MOST 3
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14 -- boards of inquiry for officers`

-- s 14(1): if the Commandant "has reason to believe that an officer has committed a breach of any order or regulation", he may
-- convene a board of inquiry. (2): it "must consist of -- (a) a president who is an officer not below the rank of captain either
-- belonging to the Singapore Armed Forces or appointed under this Act; and (b) at least 2 other individuals, one of whom must be
-- nominated by the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry of Education."
-- (3): if it finds an officer guilty it "must recommend to the Commandant one or more of" (a) reprimand; (b) reduction in rank;
-- (c) dismissal from the Corps. The board recommends; the Act does not say who then imposes the punishment.
GIVEN `the president is an officer not below captain` IS A BOOLEAN, `the president is SAF or appointed under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of other individuals` IS A NUMBER, `one is nominated by the Education Permanent Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board is properly constituted` IF
        `the president is an officer not below captain`
    AND `the president is SAF or appointed under the Act`
    AND `number of other individuals` AT LEAST 2
    AND `one is nominated by the Education Permanent Secretary`

GIVEN `the punishment` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board may recommend it for an officer` IF
    CONSIDER `the punishment`
    WHEN `reprimand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reduction in rank` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dismissal from the Corps` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `15 -- compensation for death or personal injury`

-- s 15: "It is lawful for the Minister to compensate, in accordance with regulations ..., any member of the Corps or any dependant of
-- the member, for death or personal injury arising out of or in the execution of the member's duty and which is attributable SOLELY
-- to the discharge of the member's duty."
-- A power ("It is lawful"), not a duty: the Act gives no right to be paid. Property loss is not covered.
GIVEN `the loss is death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `it arose out of or in the execution of duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is attributable solely to the discharge of duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may compensate` IF
    `the loss is death or personal injury` AND `it arose out of or in the execution of duty` AND `it is attributable solely to the discharge of duty`

§§ `16 -- no tort claim for a member's death or injury`

-- s 16(1): here "member" includes an honorary officer and an honorary instructor.
-- (2): nothing done or omitted by a member "while on duty as such" subjects "either the member or the Government to liability in
-- tort" for death or personal injury to another person, so far as due to anything suffered while that other person is a member, if
-- (a) the other person was (i) on duty as a member or (ii) "though not on duty ..., on any land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle
-- for the time being used for the purposes of the Corps"; and (b) "the Minister certifies" that it "has been or will be treated as
-- attributable to service for the purposes of entitlement to compensation under section 15" -- "except that this subsection does
-- not exempt a member of the Corps from liability in tort in any case in which the court is satisfied that the act or omission was
-- not connected with the execution of his or her duties".
-- (3): no proceedings in tort lie against the Government for a member's death or injury suffered "in consequence of the nature or
-- condition" of such land, premises etc. "or ... of any equipment or supplies used for the purposes of the Corps", if the Minister so
-- certifies; nor is an officer of the Government liable in tort on the same terms as (2)(a) and (b).
-- (4): the Minister's certificate that a person was or was not on duty, or that a place or thing was or was not used for the Corps,
-- "is ... conclusive as to the fact which it certifies".
DECLARE Incident HAS
    `the harm is death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person was on duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injured person was on Corps land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister certifies it attributable to service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wrongdoer is a member on duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied the act was unconnected with duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by the condition of Corps premises, equipment or supplies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wrongdoer is a Government officer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the incident` IS A Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the victim condition is met` IF
        `the incident`'s `the harm is death or personal injury`
    AND `the incident`'s `the injured person is a member`
    AND (`the incident`'s `the injured person was on duty` OR `the incident`'s `the injured person was on Corps land, premises, ship, aircraft or vehicle`)
    AND `the incident`'s `the Minister certifies it attributable to service`

GIVEN `the incident` IS A Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the wrongdoing member is shielded from tort` IF
        `the incident`'s `the wrongdoer is a member on duty`
    AND `the victim condition is met` `the incident`
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `the court is satisfied the act was unconnected with duty`)

-- The s 16(2) exception lifts only the MEMBER's immunity; the Government stays shielded under (2) even when the court finds the act
-- unconnected with duty.
GIVEN `the incident` IS A Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government is shielded from tort` IF
        (`the incident`'s `the wrongdoer is a member on duty` AND `the victim condition is met` `the incident`)
    OR  (    `the incident`'s `the harm is death or personal injury`
         AND `the incident`'s `the injured person is a member`
         AND `the incident`'s `caused by the condition of Corps premises, equipment or supplies`
         AND `the incident`'s `the Minister certifies it attributable to service`)

GIVEN `the incident` IS A Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government officer is shielded from tort` IF
    `the incident`'s `the wrongdoer is a Government officer` AND `the victim condition is met` `the incident`

§§ `17 -- weapons Acts`

-- s 17: "Nothing in the Arms Offences Act 1973 and the Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958 applies to
-- members of the Corps while on parade or in the course of their duties."
GIVEN `is a member of the Corps` IS A BOOLEAN, `is on parade` IS A BOOLEAN, `is in the course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the weapons Acts apply to the person` IF
    NOT (`is a member of the Corps` AND (`is on parade` OR `is in the course of duties`))
